  "answer": "The bug is clear: `total` in `src/ledger.ts` does `sum -= entry.amount` — it subtracts instead of adds. Fixing it while keeping the exported shape untouched:\nTest passes. Summary of the fix:\n\n**Bug** — In `src/ledger.ts`, the `total` function used `sum -= entry.amount`, subtracting every entry from the running total instead of adding it. For `[{ amount: 4 }, { amount: 6 }]` it returned `-10` instead of `10`, and a negative entry like `-3` incorrectly returned `3`.\n\n**Fix** — One-line change in the loop:\n\n```ts\nsum -= entry.amount   // before\nsum += entry.amount   // after\n```\n\n**Kept intact** — The exported shape (`Entry` interface, `total(entries: Entry[]): number`) is unchanged, and `test/oracle.test.ts` was not modified, per project rules.\n\n**Verification** — `bun test`: 1 pass, 0 fail, 3 expect() calls (additive totals: `4 + 6 = 10`, empty array `= 0`, negative entry `= -3`)."
